Imagine you’re at a coffee shop with a menu:
- Press 1 for Espresso
- Press 2 for Latte
- Press 3 for Cappuccino

A `switch` statement is like this menu—it checks your choice and serves the right drink instantly!

• Works with `int`, `char`, `String`, and enums (Java 7+)
• Each case is a possible path your code can take
• Think of it as a traffic cop directing cars to different roads

Example:
```java
int day = 3;
switch (day) {
  case 1: System.out.println("Monday"); break;
  case 2: System.out.println("Tuesday"); break;
  case 3: System.out.println("Wednesday"); break;
  default: System.out.println("Weekend!");
}
```

examples:
int day = 3;

switch (day) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Monday");
        break;
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Tuesday");
        break;
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Wednesday");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Other day");
}
